      "writtenOn": "2026-09-12T09:40:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The direction looks good to me, but I found one upgrade-compatibility gap: existing sites may already have accountPatchReviewDb.url configured with the previously documented jdbc:h2:file: prefix. With this patch, those sites would continue using H2\u0027s default file filesystem and would not get the async filesystem mitigation.\n\nThere was also a startup regression for sites combining that legacy URL with accountPatchReviewDb.h2LockType \u003d jgit, because lockTargetFromUrl() only accepted jdbc:h2:async:.\n\nI uploaded a follow-up change 630181 that normalizes legacy jdbc:h2:file: account patch review URLs to jdbc:h2:async:, keeps the jgit-lock parser compatible with both prefixes, adds unit coverage, and adds an end-to-end test for starting the jgit-lock store from a legacy file URL.\n\nFeel free to squash it into this change if you prefer.",
      "parentUuid": "451718aa_87eb0ef9",
